 ° 48 ′ E). The precise location for this single known occurrence of the species is not known, but it was described as occurring on western slopes in woodland on gneiss, at an altitude of 1400 – 1500 m. However, the eastern edge of the Itremo Massif protected area (status: Harmonious Protected Landscape, designated in April 2015) lies only 23 km to the west of Ambatofinandrahana and it is likely that the species was collected in this area. Nevertheless, a moderate level of botanical exploration has been undertaken in this vicinity, and the species is not known to have been collected again – it is clearly rare, or possibly even extinct.","","text","",""]]},"W4FQ":{"d":[["Colombia (Antioquia); Ecuador; Peru; Bolivia (La Paz)","","text","",""]]},"X8ZX":{"d":[["Australian(Western Australia)","","text","",""]]},"X99X":{"d":[["Philippines","","text","native",""]]},"YPGR":{"d":[["SE-Tibet","","text","",""]]},"YWY9":{"d":[["S-Greece (Peloponnisos)","","text","",""]]},"ZQC4":{"d":[["Brazil (Goiás, Minas Gerais)","","text","",""]]}}